# End-to-end EMULATOR test for a synthetic SAMD21G18 (Cortex-M0+)
# printer in DETERMINISTIC TICK MODE. Boots klipper firmware under
# Renode against a realistically-shaped cartesian pin map, completes
# klippy identify + clocksync against the TC4-driven firmware clock,
# brings up the full MCU config (4 TMC2209s on multi-drop UART, 2
# software-PWM heaters, a fan, endstops, 2 thermistors), reads the
# thermistors through the SAMD21 ADC, round-trips the four TMC2209
# register files over their shared software UART, and exercises
# interactive gcode.
#
# There is no shipped config/ board for the SAMD21G18, so this is the
# SAMD21 per-printer test in spirit: it drives the chip through the same
# TMC-UART + ADC infrastructure the real-board per-printer tests use,
# where samd21_smoke only covers boot. What it adds over the smoke test:
#
#   - TMC2209 MULTI-DROP UART (uart_pin PA6 / tx_pin PA7, uart_address
#     0..3), reusing the renode_hooks sw_uart responder. _drive_rx drives
#     the firmware RX bit through the SAMD21 PORT model (gpio_a.OnGPIO).
#     This is the first SAMD-family sw_uart test, so it also exercises
#     the renode_hooks CPU resolver fix: the SAMD repls name the CPU
#     `cpu0` (not `cpu`), and the tmcuart PC hooks now attach to either.
#     DUMP_TMC below reads the live register file for stepper_x and the
#     extruder; the IOIN read returning version=0x21 proves the
#     multi-drop UART read path round-tripped.
#
#   - The SAMD21 ADC, served by the new test/emulator/samd21_adc_stub.py
#     (the SAMD21 ADC register map differs from the SAMX5 one). The
#     hotend reads through channel index 4 (PA4) and the bed through
#     index 5 (PA5). With a broken ADC both heaters sit at temp=0.0 with
#     no shutdown, so the "temp=3" assertion (both read ~36 C) is the
#     positive proof the ADC delivered samples.
#
# Host link is SERCOM0 on PA10/PA11 (samd21g18-serial build). The gated
# path is motion-free.
DICTIONARY samd21g18.dict
CONFIG samd21_printer.cfg
EMULATOR samd21_printer.fixture.json
REQUIRES_EMULATOR  # deterministic-time lockstep needs the real backend

# Interactive gcode round-trip against real firmware in tick mode.
M114
M105
# Read back the live TMC register file over the multi-drop UART for the
# first and last drivers (uart_address 0 and 3).
DUMP_TMC STEPPER=stepper_x
DUMP_TMC STEPPER=extruder

# klippy connected, loaded the dictionary, and built the full config
# against real firmware.
EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "Loaded MCU 'mcu'"
EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "Configured MCU 'mcu'"
# DUMP_TMC dumped the first and last drivers; the IOIN read returning the
# TMC version byte (0x21) proves the multi-drop UART read path returned
# framed, CRC-valid responses for both addresses.
EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "DUMP_TMC stepper_x"
EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "DUMP_TMC extruder"
EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "version=0x21"
# Positive proof the SAMD21 ADC delivered samples: both thermistors read
# ~36 C, so a periodic Stats line carries "temp=3x". A broken ADC leaves
# them at temp=0.0 with no shutdown.
EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "temp=3"
# A broken UART round-trip surfaces as a TMC init failure or a read error.
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "failed to init"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Unable to read tmc uart"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Unable to write tmc uart"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Internal error"
# A renode-side crash (wrong sysbus peripheral, hook callback error)
# kills serial; klippy then gets EOF and identify / TMC init time out.
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Got EOF when reading from device"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "failed to init: Timeout"
# With the deterministic clock the config / TMC / ADC path pushes no
# deadline into the firmware's past, so nothing shuts down.
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "ADC out of range"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Timer too close"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Rescheduled timer in the past"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Klippy is shutdown"
